From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hayaksi1 <193020925+hayaksi1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:55:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Move the preferences-tab test where the runner can see it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This suite sat under the legacy test tree, which the vitest config never
globs, so it had not run since the co-location migration. Its snapshot was
consequently frozen at whatever upstream last wrote, and the two fork rows
that belong there — the full-size thread preference and the in-room search
shortcut help — were simply absent with nothing to notice.

Relocating it rather than hand-patching the snapshot is what makes the
coverage real: regenerating from a suite that actually executes puts both
rows in by construction, and any future row that goes missing now fails
somewhere a person will see. Ported to the vitest idiom on the way across,
and the stale jest-era snapshot key dropped since nothing keys off it now.

The rest of that legacy directory is left alone; it needs its own decision.
